{
  "id": "ts-vitest-regression",
  "title": "Off-by-one in the volume discount threshold after moving it to config",
  "description": "PR #418 moves the volume-discount threshold and rate from constants in src/pricing/discount.ts into env-driven config. While rewriting qualifiesForVolumeDiscount it changed `subtotal >= VOLUME_DISCOUNT_THRESHOLD` into `subtotal > pricingConfig.volumeDiscount.threshold`, so a subtotal of exactly 100 no longer gets the 10% discount. Vitest (verbose reporter) fails exactly one parametrized case, 'charges 90 for a 100 subtotal' (expected 100 to be 90), among 41 passing tests; the cases on either side of the boundary (99.99 and 100.01) pass, the README line removed by the PR and the unchanged doc comment both say 'or more' / 'at or above'. lint and typecheck pass (the change is type-correct) and deploy-preview is skipped because it needs test. Correct answer: a code regression in src/pricing/discount.ts; restore `>=` in qualifiesForVolumeDiscount. Changing the test expectation would be wrong because the documented behaviour is inclusive.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "shop-api"
  },
